ygorl: make observable iteration order independent of heap addresses.

Several core containers are std::unordered_set/map keyed by card*/effect*,
so iterating them follows pointer hashes. When the loop emits messages or
removes effects, two duels with the same seed and responses can produce
differently ordered message streams (seen with MSG_CARD_HINT/PLAYER_HINT
when effects reset). This patch visits those containers in a stable order:
effects by (id, initial_id, code, type, description), cards by cardid.

Applied by cmake/ocgcore.cmake to a build-tree copy of third_party/ygopro-core.

